++### Specialized link names and native texture accounting
++
++`pipeline::LinkedFunction::with_specialized_name` exports a function under an alias while
++retaining its source definition and constant values. The alias and source name both enter
++compile keys and function-table identities. `pipeline::LinkedSource::with_specialized_name`
++provides the same behavior for bitcode inputs. The runtime's `FunctionDescriptor.specialized_name`
++and `Function::with_specialized_name` preserve that alias through `linked_function()`.
++
++`Texture::backing_allocation_size` reports the Vulkan backing allocation for a native frontend.
++Heap textures report their reserved range; buffer textures report their buffer length. Unowned
++and sparse images report zero. `Texture::allocated_size` retains its Metal heap-layout semantics.
+diff --git a/docs/FAST-PATHS.md b/docs/FAST-PATHS.md
+index 4c48539..dad1620 100644
+--- a/docs/FAST-PATHS.md
++++ b/docs/FAST-PATHS.md
+@@ -108,6 +108,11 @@ known. The rest of the differences are docs/API.md section 9's precision notes.
+ 
+ ## Costs of matching Metal
+ 
++Dynamically indexed constant tables larger than 4 KiB use the pipeline's shared constant
++buffer. Smaller typed tables stay in private storage while they fit the private-memory limit.
++Constant GEP and pointer-cast expressions retain their byte offsets in either representation.
++This storage choice preserves values and avoids a private copy of a large table per invocation.
++
+ Where matching what Metal observably does costs time, the runtime matches it and the cost is
+ recorded here.
+ 
